  ],
  "question": {
    "text": "The IUPAC name of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></math> is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lS4Xd",
      "text": "Potassium tris(oxalato)cobaltate<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>III</mi></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "x9rj3",
      "text": "Potassium tris(oxalato)cobalt<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3Q8dK",
      "text": "Potassium trioxalatocobalt<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3awFX",
      "text": "Potassium trioxalatocobaltate<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>III</mi></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Ligands that include a numerical prefix in the name use the prefixes bis for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>, tris for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>, or tetrakis for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> to indicate their number.</p><p>If the complex ion is an anion, we drop the ending of the metal name and add &ndash;ate.</p><p>In the given coordination compound, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Co</mi></math> is the cobalt metal,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>&nbsp;are the ligands named as oxalato.</p><p>The charge on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and oxalate is having&nbsp;charge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the IUPAC&nbsp;name of the compound&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></math>&nbsp;is Potassium trioxalatocobaltate<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
